# XSH tcsetwinsize()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Terminal tests use a pseudo-terminal (XSI). SIGWINCH goes to the foreground group of the
# controlling terminal; the test therefore runs in a session leader that has acquired the
# pseudo-terminal as controlling terminal (implementation-defined, UNRESOLVED if it does not
# happen) and accepts the signal with sigtimedwait(). That an unchanged size raises no signal is
# checked after a first, changing call has been seen to raise one.

assertion  XSH.tcsetwinsize.001
anchor     functions/tcsetwinsize.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/tcsetwinsize.html#RETURN VALUE
class      conditional
when       BASE|XSI
since      2024
says       tcsetwinsize() with 25 rows and 81 columns returns 0 and
           tcgetwinsize() immediately shows them; so does a second call with 50
           rows and 132 columns.
note       XSI only for the pseudo-terminal set-up (posix_openpt() and its
           companions are XSI); the requirement itself is Base. A set-up that is
           not available is UNRESOLVED, or NOTINUSE when the facility is absent.
test       t/001-set-get.c

assertion  XSH.tcsetwinsize.002
anchor     functions/tcsetwinsize.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       BASE|XSI
since      2024
says       In the foreground process group of the controlling terminal, a
           tcsetwinsize() that changes the size returns 0 and SIGWINCH is
           delivered to the group (accepted within 2 s).
note       XSI only for the pseudo-terminal set-up (posix_openpt() and its
           companions are XSI); the requirement itself is Base. A set-up that is
           not available is UNRESOLVED, or NOTINUSE when the facility is absent.
timeout    40
test       t/002-sigwinch.c

assertion  XSH.tcsetwinsize.003
anchor     functions/tcsetwinsize.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       BASE|XSI
since      2024
says       A tcsetwinsize() that sets the size the terminal already has returns 0
           and delivers no SIGWINCH to the foreground group (none within 500 ms),
           after a first call that changed the size did deliver one.
note       XSI only for the pseudo-terminal set-up (posix_openpt() and its
           companions are XSI); the requirement itself is Base. A set-up that is
           not available is UNRESOLVED, or NOTINUSE when the facility is absent.
           A set-up that gets no signal for the first, changing call is
           UNRESOLVED (assertion 002 covers it).
timeout    40
test       t/003-no-sigwinch-same.c

assertion  XSH.tcsetwinsize.004
anchor     functions/tcsetwinsize.html#ERRORS/EBADF
class      required
since      2024
says       tcsetwinsize(-1) and tcsetwinsize() of a closed descriptor return -1
           with EBADF.
test       t/004-ebadf.c

assertion  XSH.tcsetwinsize.005
anchor     functions/tcsetwinsize.html#ERRORS/ENOTTY
class      required
since      2024
says       tcsetwinsize() of descriptors for a regular file, both ends of a pipe
           and /dev/null returns -1 with ENOTTY.
test       t/005-enotty-file.c

assertion  XSH.tcsetwinsize.006
anchor     functions/tcsetwinsize.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       BASE|XSI
since      2024
says       A process in a background process group (not orphaned) whose SIGTTOU
           is neither blocked nor ignored and which calls tcsetwinsize()
           (changing the row count) on its controlling terminal is sent SIGTTOU
           (default action: stopped).
note       XSI only for the pseudo-terminal set-up (posix_openpt() and its
           companions are XSI); the requirement itself is Base. A set-up that is
           not available is UNRESOLVED, or NOTINUSE when the facility is absent.
timeout    40
test       t/006-bg-sigttou.c

assertion  XSH.tcsetwinsize.007
anchor     functions/tcsetwinsize.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       BASE|XSI
since      2024
says       A process in a background process group which calls tcsetwinsize()
           (changing the row count) on its controlling terminal while SIGTTOU is
           blocked, and again while it is ignored, completes normally (returns
           0), is not stopped and the change is made.
note       XSI only for the pseudo-terminal set-up (posix_openpt() and its
           companions are XSI); the requirement itself is Base. A set-up that is
           not available is UNRESOLVED, or NOTINUSE when the facility is absent.
timeout    60
test       t/007-bg-quiet.c

assertion  XSH.tcsetwinsize.008
anchor     functions/tcsetwinsize.html#ERRORS/EIO
class      conditional
when       BASE|XSI
since      2024
says       A process in an orphaned process group, with SIGTTOU neither blocked
           nor ignored, which calls tcsetwinsize() (changing the row count) on
           its controlling terminal gets -1 with EIO.
note       XSI only for the pseudo-terminal set-up (posix_openpt() and its
           companions are XSI); the requirement itself is Base. A set-up that is
           not available is UNRESOLVED, or NOTINUSE when the facility is absent.
timeout    40
test       t/008-orphan-eio.c
